    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d983">

                <pb facs="0959" n="701" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg701"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.731/268</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 21, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1007. From American Legation, Copenhagen:</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>Owing to great quantity merchandise necessary to be imported from the United
                        States on account of other sources supply being cut off, it is necessary to
                        do business by telegraph. British censor holding up commercial telegrams
                        between Denmark and United States. This is killing business.</p>
                </quote>
                <p>Department also has telegram from Consul General, Copenhagen, same subject,
                    stating has cabled you. Please bring matter immediate attention Foreign
                    Office.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
